# ------------------------------------------------------------------ assets/
# EVERYTHING gitignored lives here, and nothing else is ignored. ~4.3 GB, and
# every byte of it is rebuilt by a script — so it can be deleted wholesale and
# restored with three commands:
#
#   pnpm import:ocg          → assets/ocgcore/  (Lua card scripts + carddata,
#                              at the commits pinned in engine/ocgcore.lock.json)
#   pnpm build:images        → assets/cards/    (full card art, {passcode}.jpg)
#                              assets/art/      (cropped artwork)
#                              assets/sets/images/ (set logos)
#   pnpm build:set-images    → assets/sets/<type>/ (official box art)
#
# A fresh clone has no card art and cannot run a duel until those have run.
#
# NOTE the leading slash: it anchors this to the repo root. A bare `assets/`
# would match ANY directory named "assets" at any depth and would silently
# swallow ui/assets/ — the one folder of hand-made art that cannot be rebuilt.
/assets/

# What is deliberately NOT here, because no script can rebuild it:
#   ui/assets/         hand-made render assets — card-frame templates, sleeves,
#                      fonts, logos. The renderer imports a sleeve at build time.
#   engine/cards/, engine/sets/       card + set databases
#   engine/banlists/, engine/genesys/ append-only archives that upstream will
#                      NEVER re-serve — only the current list is published, so a
#                      lost revision is lost for good.
#   engine/ocgcore.lock.json          the pin that makes assets/ocgcore/ safe to
#                      throw away.
#
# This is a PRIVATE repo and must stay private; never push to a public mirror.
